\section{Choosing which duplicate to keep}{

Rows are ranked, and the best in each group is kept:
\itemize{
\item \code{prefer = "original"} (default): fewest version flags (so \code{"Help!"}
beats \code{"Help! - Remastered 2009"}), then studio album over EP, single,
live, compilation, and soundtrack; then earliest release; then most
pageviews.
\item \code{prefer = "earliest"}: earliest release date first.
\item \code{prefer = "popular"}: most pageviews first.
}

Songs with no other version are always kept by \code{distinct_songs()}. For
example, if Genius only has \code{"Help! - Remastered 2009"}, that row stays. To
drop a category outright, name it in \code{remove}.
